Launch plan for repo-fixer (dry run: nothing was created)
  target         local (6f1d2c3b4a5968778695a4b3c2d1e0f1)
  access         profile python-dev version 3 (digest ffffffffffffffff)
  mode           session, lifetime 1h, expires 2026-10-24T13:00:00Z if queued now (the lifetime starts when the launch is queued)
  image          agentgate-coding@sha256:cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
  command        claude --print "fix the failing tests"
  workdir        /var/lib/agentgate/workspace
  spec digest    aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
  policy digest  bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb

What this agent may do
  network           default deny; IPv6 deny
  web               https to public addresses
  dns               1.1.1.1
  taskboard         10.0.0.1:8443
  read              /usr, /lib, /var/lib/agentgate/mounts/repo
  write             /var/lib/agentgate/workspace, /tmp
  execute           /usr/bin, /usr/local/bin
  denied            /etc/shadow
  devices           /dev/null, /dev/urandom
  signals           SIGTERM (own process tree only)
  anonymous exec    no
  mount repo        /srv/repos/app -> /var/lib/agentgate/mounts/repo (read-only, live)
  secret anthropic  $ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL = broker for api.anthropic.com (header x-api-key; the value never enters the sandbox)

Approval: required
  - brokered secrets anthropic
  - live host folder repo
  - the profile requires approval
  A different human with the approver role decides it (agentgate approve ID); never the requester.

Notices
  - kernel_verified is false: this enforcement has not been verified on a BPF LSM kernel
